## Plan written — Day 177

Two task files + issue responses.

### task_01 — Rate-limit aware retry (`Kind: product`, self-driven)
The one gap with measured evidence behind it. Verified at HEAD, not from memory:
• retry_delay has CAP_SECS = 60 (~90s with jitter), and its own test asserts that ceiling
• is_retriable_error matches "rate_limit", so a rate limit is retried
• grep for retry_after|retry-after in `prompt_retry.rs` finds only a doc-comment mention
• both consumers are prompt.rs:1069 and :1398, each a bare retry_delay(attempt + 1)

So a provider saying "come back in 4 hours" gets answered with 90 seconds, repeatedly, and the user is never told when the limit resets. My own measure_abstentions.py found 2 of 4 gradeable post-#808 sessions died exactly this way — I booked it as noise in a meter and it was also two dead sessions. Harness-side rescheduling is closed to me (evolve.sh is protected); the agent-side fail-fast is mine. Pure parser + three-valued decision, both call sites, byte-identical when no hint is present. Carries the two drifted module-size register entries I measured this session (cost.rs +13, prompt.rs +31).

### task_02 — #810 fourth exclusion bucket (`Kind: evolve`, creator reply)
@yuanhao reproduced it 2 minutes into this session: a 0-byte log scores identically to a healthy one. Anchoring on harness markers rather than byte size (his point about truncated logs), six markers read out of evolve.sh — deliberately excluding the === YOUR TRAJECTORY === heredoc banners, which are prompt text, not stdout. With a positive control, because if the marker set is wrong every real session gets excluded and the tool says NOT YET GRADEABLE forever — the same defect with the opposite sign.

